{
 "about": "Official Fenton 2025 Birth size evaluation z-scores for made-up head circumferences and lengths at 33 to 41 4/7 weeks, the source of FENTON_LENGTH_BIRTH_LMS and FENTON_HC_BIRTH_LMS in data.js and the reference set for test/verify-fenton-birth-length-hc-1116.cjs. No value here belongs to an infant: each was read off the app's growth-monitoring curve (FENTON_LENGTH_GROWTH_LMS, FENTON_HC_GROWTH_LMS) near a centile.",
 "source": {
  "calculator": "Fenton 2025 Growth Plotter, Tanis Fenton, University of Calgary",
  "url": "https://fentongrowth.ca/",
  "request": "Rows pasted into the page's \"Paste data\" box as CSV (sex, data type BirthSize, GA, head, length), then the page's \"Calculate z-scores\" button (POST /api/Fenton/DownloadCsv, 200 OK). The text under \"raw\" is the result table the page showed, cell by cell, tab-joined; the SHA-256 of JSON.stringify(raw) computed in the page was 3208da8b727dedba0083981e6e1812950d91384ccc529d833351736b638fdfe2 and matched this file.",
  "version": "2.1.3.0",
  "versionSource": "The page footer, \"API Software Version\"",
  "retrieved": "2026-11-16",
  "approvedBy": "Pp, in chat on 2026-11-16 (\"ถามเครื่องคิดเลข Fenton\", then \"เริ่มเลย\"), for a round of made-up birth-size head and length values at 36 to 42 weeks, both sexes",
  "sent": "Sex, data type Birth size evaluation, and per row GA, head and length. No name, number, title, date of birth, GA at birth or weight.",
  "design": "Three rows per whole week, 33 to 42, near the growth-monitoring curve's 10th, 50th and 90th; 33 to 35 were added to see where the two curves part. The 42-week rows were not returned, and probes found the last GA the evaluation accepts is 41 4/7, so three rows were asked there to close the curve. Nine held-out rows per sex at half weeks 33.5 to 41.5 (near the 3rd or 97th) and the probes are not used to build any row."
 },
